content:
The cuboid is \(3\times 3\times 2\), so it has 18 small cubes. Each coloured piece has 6 cubes.

Tracking the visible white cubes shows that:
- the white square on the front forces the hidden cube directly behind it to be white;
- the white square on the right side forces the hidden cube to its left to be white;
- the white square on the top also connects through the first hidden white cube;
- the last hidden white cube must be the one on the left, otherwise the dark piece would be disconnected.

Thus the white piece has one central cube with three single-cube “arms” and one arm that is two cubes long. This is exactly the shape in Diagram A.

